div
  / Desktop: the table grows with its rows and the page scrolls. Phones: with the
  / KPI rail gone, the table becomes its own capped scroll area (offset only by
  / the fixed nav, so no content-dependent guessing), which lets the heading row
  / and the pinned year column stay put while the figures scroll. It runs edge to
  / edge (negative margin cancels the content panel's padding) on a plain solid
  / backdrop - the backdrop is what the pinned header and year column scroll
  / behind. It only scrolls sideways when the columns get too wide.
  .overflow-x-auto class='max-md:-mx-4 max-md:max-h-[calc(100dvh-6rem-env(safe-area-inset-top)-var(--bottom-nav-offset))] max-md:bg-white dark:max-md:bg-gray-900'
    .table.min-w-full.select-text.text-sm.md:text-base.tabular-nums
      .table-header-group.text-gray-800.dark:text-gray-400
        .table-row
          / Every header carries a tooltip explaining the figure - the grouped
          / columns name the folded-in categories, so the condensed layout stays
          / self-explanatory.
          - header_columns.each do |label, hint, key|
            .table-cell.align-bottom.p-2.text-right.font-bold.whitespace-nowrap class=header_cell_class(key)
              span.cursor-help.underline.decoration-dotted.decoration-gray-300.dark:decoration-gray-600.underline-offset-4 data-controller='tooltip' title=hint
                = label

      .table-row-group.text-gray-800.dark:text-gray-300
        - rows.each_with_index do |row, index|
          / The forecast rows read at full strength (dimming them was unreadable
          / in dark mode); a dashed rule on the first projected row's cells is
          / what sets the projection apart from the measured years. The savings
          / figure is what's actually forecast, so it carries the "Prognose" hint.
          - separator = separator_class(index)
          .table-row.hover:bg-gray-100.dark:hover:bg-gray-700
            / PV years are not calendar years, so number them 1, 2, 3, ... -
            / year N is the Nth year of operation from the installation date. The
            / exact date range is one hover away in the tooltip on the number.
            .table-cell.align-middle.p-2.text-right.whitespace-nowrap.font-medium class=[separator, year_column_class]
              span.cursor-help.underline.decoration-dotted.decoration-gray-300.dark:decoration-gray-600.underline-offset-4 data-controller='tooltip' title=period_label(row)
                = index + 1
            - groups.each do |group|
              / One column per group, showing the group's net total for the year
              / as a single figure - seven sparse columns collapse into three and
              / every year stays a single calm row. The drill-down link filters
              / the cash-flow list to all of the group's categories at once. An
              / empty group shows a dash.
              - value = group_sum(row, group)
              .table-cell.align-middle.p-2.text-right.whitespace-nowrap class=[signed_color(value), separator]
                - if value && (path = group_path(row, group))
                  = link_to amount(value), path, class: 'hover:underline', data: { turbo_frame: '_top' }
                - else
                  = amount(value)
            .table-cell.align-middle.p-2.text-right.whitespace-nowrap class=[signed_color(row[:savings]), separator]
              - if (path = savings_path(row))
                = link_to amount(row[:savings]), path, class: 'hover:underline', data: { turbo_frame: '_top' }
              - elsif row[:projected]
                span.cursor-help.underline.decoration-dotted.decoration-gray-300.dark:decoration-gray-600.underline-offset-4 data-controller='tooltip' title=t('.projected')
                  = amount(row[:savings])
              - else
                = amount(row[:savings])
            .table-cell.align-middle.p-2.text-right.whitespace-nowrap class=[signed_color(row[:nominal]), separator]
              = currency(row[:nominal])
            .table-cell.align-middle.p-2.text-right.whitespace-nowrap class=[signed_color(row[:npv]), separator]
              = currency(row[:npv])
            .table-cell.align-middle.p-2.text-right.whitespace-nowrap class=separator
              = degree(row[:degree])
